 ],
 "meaning": "A viniyoga is the statement said before a mantra of its seer (ṛṣi), its metre (chandas), its deity (devatā) and the use (viniyoga) it is put to. Here: the three ṛks āpo hi ṣṭhā (TS 4.1.5.1; RV 10.9.1–3), seen by Sindhudvīpa, in the gāyatrī metre, addressed to the Waters, used for sprinkling oneself. The commas of the witness mark the pauses between the parts; a word before a comma keeps its pausal form.",
 "in_the_rite": "Step marjana, before āpo hi ṣṭhā, in all three services (M only).",
